cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ScholarScribe in your research workflow, please cite it."
title: "ScholarScribe: a privacy-first, local-LLM writing companion for researchers"
authors:
  - family-names: Mandour
    given-names: Waleed
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9262-5993"
abstract: >-
  ScholarScribe is a cross-platform desktop application for researchers that
  provides local, privacy-preserving writing assistance through Ollama-hosted
  large language models. It includes Writing Provenance, an author-side
  evidence tool that turns Word Track Changes or Google Docs revision history
  into hash-chained, Ed25519-signed export packets, an AI-use disclosure
  generator, citation-pattern inventory, and educational modules about
  AI-text detector reliability. All inference is local; the app's documented
  network surface is listed in docs/NETWORK_SURFACE.json.
keywords:
  - academic writing
  - writing provenance
  - local LLM
  - Ollama
  - research integrity
  - AI disclosure
license: MIT
